      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "Cohere2Config supplies the architecture string and Cohere2Model supplies its config_class to the existing registry comprehension. Model construction creates token embeddings, parallel decoder blocks, final LayerNorm and a scaled vocabulary projection.",
          "basis": "source",
          "evidence": ["call_3b30bab5a3cd4a8e98cbc713bb68a5d9", "call_c15fad2552ba4b42a263fed4d4ba37c1"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Each parallel block normalizes its input once, passes that same normalized tensor to attention and the gated MLP, and adds both outputs to the residual. Cohere2 supplies all three components and uses separate q_proj/k_proj/v_proj/o_proj and gate_proj/up_proj/down_proj checkpoint names.",
