          "evidence": ["call_89628af38f3a4bb69896593a2f7d1eb3", "call_0e83b5766f5d42ce80e20dd0e4f68904"]
        },
        {
          "text": "Local layers use GPTJ-style RoPE settings. With the inspected configurations' null rope_scaling, RoPE selects its default inverse-frequency calculation; RoPE.apply forwards the style to the native extension rather than using apply_torch. Global layers bypass this operation entirely.",
