          "evidence": ["call_c15fad2552ba4b42a263fed4d4ba37c1", "call_0dc4d904b4bf45008e023c2e84ae454b", "call_ba7d81e1302b452d84ced56cd4f795a2", "call_5eb7063d3ca641e8a6142188c0feec96"]
        },
        {
          "text": "A bounded Python transcription yields 48 local and 16 global layers for Command A, and 24 local and 8 global layers for each R7B configuration. Global layers are every fourth layer. Query projection widths are respectively 12288 and 4096; KV projection width is 1024 for all three. Hidden width divided by query-head count also yields 128 in every case, although their explicit head_dim makes that fallback unnecessary.",
